## Kept in places
// A note kept in each kind of place a Python program keeps things in (epic `data` P40):
// - a database on this device:  in a browser, its own storage;  in Python, a file beside the program
// - a data folder on the server:  each note a JSON file, in this project's `__data/notes`
// - a CSV file on the server:  this project's `__data/notes.csv`, a row each
// The restart test keeps a note in each, stops the program, runs it again, and reads them back.
this device is a database on this device

note folder is a data folder at "notes":
	- check it every 30 seconds

note sheet is a sheet at "notes.csv":
	- its id is its "id"
	- check it every 30 seconds

a "note" is a thing:
	- its "text" is text

a "device note" is a note:
	- it lives in this device

a "folder note" is a note:
	- it lives in note folder

a "sheet note" is a note:
	- it lives in note sheet

note keeper is an app:
	- its "draft" is text
	- its "device count" is a number
	- its "folder count" is a number
	- its "sheet count" is a number

	// the draft, kept in each place
	- to keep the draft:
		if the draft is "" return
		add (a new device note with text = the draft) to the device notes
		add (a new folder note with text = the draft) to the folder notes
		add (a new sheet note with text = the draft) to the sheet notes
		clear the draft

	// how many each place keeps now
	- to count the notes:
		set the device count to the length of every device note
		set the folder count to the length of every folder note
		set the sheet count to the length of every sheet note

	- to draw it:
		<ui-stack>
			<ui-form value={it}>
				<ui-input name="draft" aria-label="Note"/>
				<ui-button class="keep" onClick={keep the draft}>Keep</ui-button>
			</ui-form>
			<ui-text class="counts">{its device count} on this device, {its folder count} in the folder, {its sheet count} in the sheet</ui-text>
		</ui-stack>


## Start
// only this device's notes:  the server's need a page server, which a plain run has none of
print the length of every device note
add (a new device note with text = "a run") to the device notes
print the length of every device note
start the note keeper
